{"name":"Magical Stardust","hex":"#eaeadb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"magical","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or by means of magic.","Enchanting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magical"},{"term":"stardust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Small fragments of dustlike material found in space; specifically, a type of cosmic dust that formed from cooling gases ejected from presolar stars, which was then incorporated into the cloud from which the Solar System condensed.","Small fragments of dustlike material found in space; specifically, a type of cosmic dust that formed from cooling gases ejected from presolar stars, which was then incorporated into the cloud from which the Solar System condensed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stardust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stardust (2007 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Stardust is a 2007 romantic fantasy adventure film directed by Matthew Vaughn and co-written by Vaughn and Jane Goldman. Based on Neil Gaiman's 1999 novel, it features an ensemble cast led by Claire Danes, Charlie Cox, Sienna Miller, Ricky Gervais, Jason Flemyng, Rupert Everett, Peter O'Toole, Michelle Pfeiffer and Robert De Niro, with narration by Ian McKellen."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Stardust_promo_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stardust_(2007_film)","wikidata":"Q244398"},{"title":"Stardust (Gaiman novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Stardust is a 1999 fantasy novel by British writer Neil Gaiman, usually published with illustrations by Charles Vess. Stardust has a different tone and style from most of Gaiman's prose fiction, being consciously written in the tradition of pre-Tolkien English fantasy, following in the footsteps of authors such as Lord Dunsany and Hope Mirrlees. It is concerned with the adventures of a young man from the village of Wall, which borders the magical land of Faerie."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e1/StardustGaimanbookcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stardust_(Gaiman_novel)","wikidata":"Q1166201"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Claire_Danes_at_Much_Music_by_Robin_Wong_9.jpg/250px-Claire_Danes_at_Much_Music_by_Robin_Wong_9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/92/Claire_Danes_at_Much_Music_by_Robin_Wong_9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Claire_Danes_at_Much_Music_by_Robin_Wong_9.jpg/250px-Claire_Danes_at_Much_Music_by_Robin_Wong_9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Claire Danes promoting Stardust","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClaire_Danes_at_Much_Music_by_Robin_Wong_9.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Quiraing%2C_Isle_of_Skye.jpg/500px-Quiraing%2C_Isle_of_Skye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Quiraing%2C_Isle_of_Skye.jpg/500px-Quiraing%2C_Isle_of_Skye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Locations used in Scotland included the area surrounding the Quiraing, on the Isle of Skye.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuiraing%2C_Isle_of_Skye.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Michelle_Pfeiffer_2007.jpg/500px-Michelle_Pfeiffer_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Michelle_Pfeiffer_2007.jpg/500px-Michelle